From efc5467e71c8054bb66174d5cca2f69be14d37ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 252/254] reaper v1.8.8: Warden LAN-lockout fixes + rwatch
 watchdog + hwqos idempotence

Root-caused from the 2026-07-29 field incident (BE96U owner + GT-BE98
tester): Warden's 04:30 feed update ingested FireHOL level1 fullbogons
(192.168/16, 127/8, 0/8, ...) into rw_threat and the post-0243 chain
order dropped all NEW LAN/loopback traffic until a power cycle.

rwarden.c:
- updater: rw_f4/rw_f6 reserved-range filters on every ingested token
  (v4 private/loopback/link-local/CGNAT/multicast; v6 unspec/LL/ULA/mcast)
- chain order: structural anti-lockout restored - lo, DHCP(v4 67:68 /
  v6 546:547), ESTABLISHED, allow src, ban src, [allow dst + dst drops],
  LAN RETURN, THEN feed/geo src drops (keeps the audit-L2 property;
  whitelist now also exempts destinations in dir=out/both)
- persistence: ipset save takes ONE setname - the multi-name call wrote
  an EMPTY cache with exit 0, so boot restore had never worked; save
  per-set, install only non-empty
- validation: rw_valid_cidr now octet/prefix-strict, v6 prefix-bounded;
  rejected tokens counted+logged, runtime ipset-add failures logged

rwatch.c (new, default on): cron probe every 5 min - WAN first-hop ping
(no external hosts), loopback DNS via dnsmasq, Warden canary (LAN IP /
127.0.0.1 must never match a block set; re-applies chain + CRITICAL log
on breach), GDX skb_idx pool exhaustion (the silent accelerator-wedge
signature - stock has no watchdog). Syslog transitions; first failure
dumps bounded diagnostics (iptables/ipset/GDX/FPM/fcache/tmctl/dmesg)
to /jffs/rwatch (newest 3 kept). nvram rwatch_enable/rwatch_iv.

qos.c start_hwqos: idempotence guard (skip live-queue rewrite when
config unchanged and TM answers; wan_up re-applies destructively
otherwise) + tmctl exit codes logged, state recorded only on success.

Reaper_Warden.asp + 25 dicts: ban/whitelist entries validated (reject
whole save + alert, never silently strip/mangle); RWDN_11 rewritten to
document multi-select add/remove; new RWDN_52 (English-seeded, 5843
lockstep).

